# AFClaude manager container crontab (supercronic, container clock = UTC like the host).
# The only AFClaude schedule (the host crontab has no AFClaude lines since 01.10.); every
# Claude-side action goes through the SSH bridge (host.py). Keep the "# AFClaude ..." tags:
# export_quickview.py lists them, and runner.py matches its jobs to them (JOBS cron_tag).
# Phase 3a (docs/phase3a_plan.md): with AFCLAUDE_SCHEDULER=on the resident runner (runner.py)
# runs beside this crontab and owns the jobs in runner.RUNNER_OWNS; each cut-over step moves lines
# from here into it. S2: stall_scan, prune_runs (new, never cron lines). S3: the usage sampler, the
# dispatcher, the quickview export, the docs import, the log retention and the hourly usage review
# (their lines are gone from here; runner.JOBS has their cadences, runner_jobs.HANDLERS their
# commands, logs and flocks). S4: the at-jobs (scheduled_jobs, stored by `at -t`): the runner runs
# each at its minute as a tracked child; the */1 `at --run-due` line is gone. S5: the session-window
# starts (`keepalive.py --window-start --start-key`, to the second at each start); the */30
# `--window-start` line is gone. S6: the keep-alive watcher's passes (runner jobs watch, run_readings,
# compaction_check and their acts); the entrypoint no longer starts the watcher and its :07/:22/:37/:52
# watchdog line is gone. S7: the inbox (runner jobs inbox, inbox_verify) and the inbox API, which the
# runner keeps running as a supervised child (runner.SUPERVISED: `inbox_api.py serve --no-worker`,
# restart + alert); the entrypoint no longer starts it and its */5 `ensure` watchdog line is gone.
# docker/crontab.legacy is this file as it was before S2 (the rollback mode AFCLAUDE_SCHEDULER=legacy,
# which keeps every line, `at --run-due`, the */30 window-start, the watcher watchdog and the inbox
# API watchdog among them).
# RUNNER WATCHDOG (phase 3a S2-S7, removed in S8 when the runner is the container's main process):
# starts runner.py serve again if it is not running (an alert + pause unless its crash or unclean
# exit is reported already), and alerts a stale loop heartbeat. The entrypoint starts the runner.
*/5 * * * * cd $AFCLAUDE_DIR && python3 runner.py ensure >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/runner.log 2>&1 # AFClaude runner watchdog (no-op if running)
